From: "Scott Hanan (t2 executor)" <t3exec@t2.tailc9b568.ts.net>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 06:26:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] fix(server): stable compat interrupt retries, refuse
 onlyIfSettled, JSONC key check (#303)

Independent review NO-GO on hanan-work#817:
- a retried compat interrupt (or session.stop) no longer re-resolves the
  newest run: once any run was interrupted under the command id, the retry
  interrupts nothing
- onlyIfSettled session stops are refused (400); their check could only run
  before admission, where a new turn can slip in
- the continuation key is detected with the same lenient JSONC parser the
  settings use, so a commented explicit true is kept

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
